%I A401124 #13 Oct 22 2026 23:00:05
%S A401124 1,10,132,2341,57427,7571579
%N A401124 The number of semirings with n elements up to isomorphism.
%C A401124 A semiring is a set S with two binary operations + and x such that (S, +) is a commutative semigroup, and (S, *) is a semigroup, and multiplication distributes over addition. Note that some authors require (S, +) to have an identity 0, such that 0 * x = x * 0 = 0 for all x in S, but this requirement is not used here.
%H A401124 J. Edwards, J. D. Mitchell, and P. Ragavan, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.03709">Counting finite semirings</a>, arXiv:2507.03709 [math.RA], 2025-2026. See Table 1.
%F A401124 Since all rings are semirings, a(n) >= A027623(n).
%Y A401124 Cf. A000001, A001423, A027623, A027851, A305858.
%K A401124 nonn,more,hard,new
%O A401124 1,2
%A A401124 _James Mitchell_, Oct 15 2026
